#@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
#@type = "zendesk.integration"

Feature: OSB to Zendesk Project Name Update Integration
	Testing project sync updates in Zendesk caused by name and code changes in OSB.

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Osbzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| OSBDSKOSBDSK |
	| OSBZENOSBZEN |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| OSBDSKOSBDSK |
	| OSBZENOSBZEN |
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Osbzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: Update project name and code
	Project name and code updates should reflect in zendesk.liferay.com.

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code     | OSBZENOSBZEN                  | |
	| Language | English                       | |
	| Name     | Osbzen - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region   | United States                 | |
	| Status   | Active                        | |
	| Tier     | T1                            | |
	And I create a postal address for an account with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Country               | United States   |
	| Locality              | Diamond Bar     |
	| Region                | California      |
	| Type                  | Business        |
	| Mailing               | True            |
	| Postal Code           | 91765           |
	| Primary               | True            |
	| Street Address Line 1 | 123 Main Street |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Portal Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 6 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Gold Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the support organization with the code "OSBZENOSBZEN" should be part of the support site
	And the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	When I update a koroneiki account with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" to have the following values
	| Name         | Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Code         | OSBDSKOSBDSK                  | |
	Then the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}" should have the following parameters
	| Name         | Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Account Code | OSBDSKOSBDSK                  |
	And the support account ID of the project with the code "OSBDSKOSBDSK" should match the organization external ID on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}" should have the tag "liferay_portal"
	And the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}" should have the tag "t1"
	And the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}" should have the tag "us"
	And the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}" should have the tag "gold"
	And the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}" should have the tag "english"
	And the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}" should have the tag "approved"

Scenario: Update project name and code on expired project
	Project name and code updates should reflect in zendesk.liferay.com when the project is expired.

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code     | OSBZENOSBZEN                  | |
	| Language | English                       | |
	| Name     | Osbzen - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region   | United States                 | |
	| Status   | Active                        | |
	| Tier     | T1                            | |
	And I create a postal address for an account with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Country               | United States   |
	| Locality              | Diamond Bar     |
	| Region                | California      |
	| Type                  | Business        |
	| Mailing               | True            |
	| Postal Code           | 91765           |
	| Primary               | True            |
	| Street Address Line 1 | 123 Main Street |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Portal Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 6 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Gold Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the support organization with the code "OSBZENOSBZEN" should be part of the support site
	And the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	When I generate past static start and end dates
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Portal Production" to have the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticPastEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticPastOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticPastStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                     | |
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Gold Subscription" to have the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticPastEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticPastOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticPastStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                     | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	Then the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	When I update a koroneiki account with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" to have the following values
	| Name         | Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Code         | OSBDSKOSBDSK                  | |
	Then the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}" should have the following parameters
	| Name         | Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Account Code | OSBDSKOSBDSK                  |
	And the support account ID of the project with the code "OSBDSKOSBDSK" should match the organization external ID on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}" should not have the tag "liferay_portal"
	And the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}" should have the tag "t1"
	And the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}" should have the tag "us"
	And the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}" should not have the tag "gold"
	And the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}" should have the tag "english"
	And the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}" should have the tag "expired"
	And the organization "Osbdsk - ${staticProjectName}" should not have the tag "approved"